              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nCLOSED\n\nU.S. District Court [LIVE]\nWestern District of Texas (San Antonio)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 5:19-cr-00804-FB All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Duron Date Filed: 11/06/2019\n\nMagistrate judge case number: 5:19-mj-01188-HJB\n\nAssigned to: Judge Fred Biery\nAppeals court case number: 23-50029 (Doc. 70) 5CCA\n\nDefendant (1)\nFelipe Jesus Duron represented by Felipe Jesus Duron\n#41747480\nFederal Transfer Center\nP.O. Box 898801\nOklahoma City, OK 73189-8801\nPRO SE\n\nBernie Martinez\nBernie Martinez, Attorney at Law\n310 Tendick\nUnit 1103\nSan Antonio, TX 78209\n210-973-7539\nEmail: bernie@berniemartinezlaw.com\nTERMINATED: 08/06/2021\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nMarina Thais Douenat\nFederal Public Defender, TXW\n300 Convent Street\nSuite 2300\nSan Antonio, TX 78205\n210-472-6700\nEmail: marina_douenat@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 01/29/2021\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender\nAppointment\n\nPhilip J. Lynch\nLaw Offices of Phil Lynch\n17503 La Cantera Parkway\nSuite 104-623\nSan Antonio, TX 78257\n(210) 378-3114\nEmail: LawofficesofPhilLynch@satx.rr.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nDuty Pub. Defender-San Antonio\nFederal Public Defender\nSan Antonio Division\n300 Convent St.\nSuite 2300\nSan Antonio, TX 78205\n(210) 472-6700\nFax: 210/472-4454\nEmail: janie_craig@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 10/17/2019\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender\nAppointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2422.F - COERCION OR ENTICEMENT OF A Child Ten (10) years imprisonment to run concurrent; Five years\n(1) supervised release to run concurrent; $100 special assessment.\n18:2251.F - SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN\nFifteen (15) years imprisonment to run consecutive; Five years\nProduction of Child Pornography\nsupervised release to run concurrent;$100 special assessment.\n(2)\n18:2252A.F - ACTIVITIES RE MATERIAL\nCONSTITUTING/CONTAINING CHILD PORNO Receipt of Thirteen (13) years imprisonment to run consecutive; Five years\nChild Pornography supervised release to run concurrent; $100 special assessment.\n(3)\n18:875D.F - INTERSTATE COMMUNICATIONS -THREATS\nOne (1) year imprisonment to run consecutive; One (1) year\nTO PERSONS Extortion\nsupervised release to run concurrent; $100 special assessment.\n(4)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nNone\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Bettina J. Richardson\nAssistant U.S. Attorney\n601 NW Loop 410, Suite 600\nSan Antonio, TX 78206\n(210) 384-7152\nFax: 210/384-7118\nEmail: bettina.richardson@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nFidel Esparza , III\nUnited States Attorney's Office\nAsset Forfeiture Unit\n601 NW Loop 410, Suite 600\nSan Antonio, TX 78216\n210-384-7026\nFax: 210-384-7045\nEmail: fidel.esparza@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nJoseph H. Gay , Jr.\nFORMER Assistant U.S. Attorney\n601 N.W. Loop 410\nSuite 600\nSan Antonio, TX 78216\n(210) 384-7030\nFax: 210 384-7031\nEmail: Joseph.Gay@usdoj.gov\nTERMINATED: 03/13/2025\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n10/11/2019 1 MOTION to Seal Complaint by USA as to Felipe Jesus Duron. (bc) [5:19-mj-01188-HJB] (Entered: 10/15/2019)\n10/11/2019 2 ORDER GRANTING 1 Motion to Seal Complaint as to Felipe Jesus Duron (1). Signed by Judge Henry J. Bemporad. (bc) [5:19-mj-01188-\nHJB] (Entered: 10/15/2019)\n10/11/2019 4 MOTION to Continue, MOTION to Detain Defendant without Bond by USA as to Felipe Jesus Duron. (bc) [5:19-mj-01188-HJB] (Entered:\n10/15/2019)\n10/11/2019 5 Arrest Warrant Issued by Judge Henry J. Bemporad as to Felipe Jesus Duron. (bc) [5:19-mj-01188-HJB] (Entered: 10/15/2019)\n10/11/2019 6 REDACTED COMPLAINT