ial assessment.; Count(s) 2, Fifteen (15) years imprisonment to run consecutive; Five years\nsupervised release to run concurrent;$100 special assessment.; Count(s) 3, Thirteen (13) years imprisonment to run consecutive; Five years\nsupervised release to run concurrent; $100 special assessment.; Count(s) 4, One (1) year imprisonment to run consecutive; One (1) year\nsupervised release to run concurrent; $100 special assessment.. Signed by Judge Fred Biery. (rg) (Entered: 06/03/2021)\n06/02/2021 57 Sealed Statement of Reasons as to Felipe Jesus Duron. (SOR documents are not available electronically.) (rg) (Entered: 06/03/2021)\n07/15/2021 58 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Notice of Appeal by Felipe Jesus Duron. (rg) (Entered: 07/19/2021)\n07/15/2021 70 NOTICE OF APPEAL by Felipe Jesus Duron Per 5th Circuit rules, the appellant has 14 days, from the filing of the Notice of Appeal, to\norder the transcript. To order a transcript, the appellant should fill out a Transcript Order and follow the instructions set out on the form. If\nthe appellant has a court appointed attorney under CJA, the CJA 24 vouchers must be completed in the E-voucher system. (nm) (Entered:\n01/09/2023)\n07/27/2021 59 RESPONSE in Opposition by USA as to Felipe Jesus Duron re 58 MOTION for Extension of Time to File filed by Defendant Felipe Jesus\nDuron (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order)(Richardson, Bettina) (Entered: 07/27/2021)\n07/28/2021 60 ORDER DENYING 58 Motion for Extension of Time to File an Appeal as to Felipe Jesus Duron (1). Signed by Judge Fred Biery. (rg)\n(Entered: 07/28/2021)\n08/02/2021 61 REPLY TO RESPONSE to Motion by Felipe Jesus Duron re 58 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Appeal filed by Defendant Felipe\nJesus Duron (rg) (Entered: 08/03/2021)\n08/04/2021 62 ORDER GRANTING 58 Motion for Extension of Time to File a Notice of Appeal as to Felipe Jesus Duron (1). The Defendant has a sixty\n(60) day extension of time to file an appeal. Signed by Judge Fred Biery. (rg) (Entered: 08/04/2021)\n08/05/2021 63 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Felipe Jesus Duron. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Order Order Granting Withdrawal)(Martinez,\nBernie) (Entered: 08/05/2021)\n08/06/2021 64 ORDER GRANTING 63 Motion to Withdraw Attorney Bernie Martinez as to Felipe Jesus Duron (1). Signed by Judge Fred Biery. (rg)\n(Entered: 08/06/2021)\n08/06/2021 Attorney Bernie Martinez terminated as to Felipe Jesus Duron. (rg) (Entered: 08/06/2021)\n08/09/2021 65 MOTION for Reconsideration re 60 Order on Motion for Extension of Time to File Appeal by Felipe Jesus Duron. (rg) (Entered:\n08/10/2021)\n03/14/2022 67 PRO-SE MOTION for Leave to File (2255 Motion) by Felipe Jesus Duron. (wg) (Entered: 03/14/2022)\n03/14/2022 Updated Address per Filing as to Felipe Jesus Duron (wg) (Entered: 03/14/2022)\n03/14/2022 68 Letter/Correspondence by Felipe Jesus Duron (wg) (Entered: 03/14/2022)\n01/06/2023 69 ORDER as to Felipe Jesus Duron, GRANTED 65 MOTION for Reconsideration re 60 Order on Motion for Extension of Time to File filed\nby Felipe Jesus Duron, DISMISSED 67 MOTION for Leave to File 2255 filed by Felipe Jesus Duron., Attorney Philip J. Lynch for Felipe\nJesus Duron added. Signed by Judge Fred Biery. (nm) (Entered: 01/09/2023)\n01/20/2023 71 ORDER APPOINTING COUNSEL as to Felipe Jesus Duron Philip J. Lynch for Felipe Jesus Duron appointed.. Signed by Judge Richard\nB. Farrer. (nm) (Entered: 01/23/2023)\n01/24/2023 72 TRANSCRIPT REQUEST by Felipe Jesus Duron for dates of July 14, 2020; May 18, 2021 before Judge Hon. Fred Biery,. Proceedings\nTranscribed: Rearraingment/Plea; Sentencing. Court Reporter: Chris Poage. re 70 Notice of Appeal - Final Judgment,, (Lynch, Philip)\n(Entered: 01/24/2023)\n02/08/2023 73 TRANSCRIPT filed of Proceedings as to Felipe Jesus Duron held on 7/14/2020 Proceedings Transcribed: Rearraignment/Plea Hearing (By\nVideo). Court Reporter/Transcriber Chris Poage, Telephone number (210)244-5036 Email: chris_poage@txwd.uscourts.gov. Parties are\nnotified of their duty to review the transcript to ensure compliance with the FRCP 5.2(a)/FRCrP 49.1(a). A copy may be purchased from the\ncourt reporter or viewed at the clerk's office public terminal. If redaction is necessary, a Notice of Redaction Request must be filed within\n21 days. If no such Notice is filed, the transcript will be made available via PACER without redaction after 90 calendar days. The clerk will\nmail a copy of this notice to parties not electronically noticed. Redaction Request due 3/1/2023, Redacted Transcript Deadline set for\n3/13/2023, Release of Transcript Restriction set for 5/9/2023, Appeal Record due by 2/23/2023, (cp) (Entered: 02/08/2023)\n02/08/2023 74 TRANSCRIPT filed of Proceedings as to Felipe Jesus Duron held on 5/18/2021 Proceedings Transcribed: Sentencing Hearing (By Video).\nCourt Reporter/Transcriber Chris Poage, Telephone number (210)244-5036 Email: chris_poage@txwd.uscourts.gov. Parties are notified of\ntheir duty to review the transcript to ensure compliance with the FRCP 5.2(a)/FRCrP 49.1(a). A copy may be purchased from the court\nreporter or viewed at the clerk's office public terminal. If redaction is necessary, a Notice of Redaction Request must be filed within 21\ndays. If no such Notice is filed, the transcript will be made available via PACER without redaction after 90 calendar days. The clerk will\nmail a copy of this notice to parties not electronically noticed. Redaction Request due 3/1/2023, Redacted Transcript Deadline set for\n3/13/2023, Release of Transcript Restriction set for 5/9/2023, Appeal Record due by 2/23/2023, (cp) (Entered: 02/08/2023)\n03/03/2023 Certification of the Electronic Record on Appeal in USCA #23-50029 has been accepted by the 5th Circuit as to Felipe Jesus Duron. re 70\nNotice of Appeal - Final Judgment. Attorneys are advised that they may now download the EROA from the Fifth Circuit CM/ECF site.\nPlease click this link to download the instructions here (dtg) (Entered: 03/03/2023)\n03/29/2023 75 JUDGMENT/MANDATE of USCA (certified copy) as to Felipe Jesus Duron. Terminated appeal: 70 Notice of Appeal - Final\nJudgment.***CLERKS OFFICE: Under Fed. R. App. P. 42(b), the appeal is dismissed as of March 29, 2023, pursuant to Appellants\nunopposed motion.*** (Attachments: # 1 TRANSMITTAL LETTER FROM USCA5)(dtg) (Entered: 03/29/2023)\n\nPACER Service Center\nTransaction Receipt\n06/28/2026 21:40:56\nPACER\nmrinaal_ramachandran Client Code:\nLogin:\nSearch 5:19-cr-00804-\nDescription: Docket Report\nCriteria: FB\nBillable\n9 Cost: 0.90\nPages:"
